Subject: [PATCH] TEMPORARY: log FleeManager::isUseful()'s real decision

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS, AND WHY IT IS TEMPORARY

Even with 0007 (critical-health-out-of-combat-retreat) deployed, the wow-dev
family's death loop did not stop - confirmed live, ~6 deaths/character/10min,
unchanged. Earlier diagnostic logging (now removed) proved RetreatFromDanger-
Action::Execute() fires correctly but FleeManager::isUseful() returns false,
so the action bails before ever calling CalculateDestination().

Five independently-queried AI models all guessed isUseful() gates on whether
a flee DESTINATION exists (terrain/navmesh reasoning). Reading the actual
pinned source (src/Mgr/Move/FleeManager.cpp) shows this is wrong: isUseful()
never touches destinations. It only asks whether anything in "possible
targets no los" is within its own GetAttackDistance() of the bot's
startPosition - a question about whether fleeing is warranted at all, not
whether it is possible.

GetAttackDistance (core AzerothCore, Creature.cpp) is the aggro/detection
radius, not melee reach - base 20yd, growing ~1yd per level the player is
under the creature, capped at 25yd under. Against a much-higher-level
Flamescale Wyrmkin, that is close to the 45yd ceiling, which should make this
check trivially true if the creature is anywhere near the bot. So this
should not be failing - and finding out WHY it does anyway is the point of
this patch.

This is instrumentation only, no behavior change: logs the candidate count,
each candidate's name/entry/distance/attackDistance, and which branch is
taken. DELETE THIS PATCH in the same commit as whatever real fix the logs
point to - it is not meant to ship.

APPLIES TO: mod-playerbots @ 8d9f6aa6bc6d45f9ae0ee0675b9b1f8aa6937312,
src/Mgr/Move/FleeManager.cpp, after 0001-0007.

